            "points": "Investigation 1 | In-Vitro Anti-Fibrotic Mechanism | Investigate relevant cellular biological activity and generate preliminary anti-fibrotic evidence.\nInvestigation 2 | Molecular Mechanism & Biomarkers | Investigate relevant molecular pathways and fibrosis-associated biomarkers.\nInvestigation 3 | Histopathology & Tissue Remodelling | Investigate whether biological activity corresponds to measurable structural and tissue-level changes.\nPlanning | Human Clinical Development Planning | Develop the protocol, population, endpoints, comparator, sample size, ethics, registration and study procedures for human fibrosis-remodelling research.\nInvestigation 4 | Human OSMF Fibrosis-Remodelling / Reversal Study | A separate investigation designed to evaluate clinical, biological and tissue-level outcomes in patients with established OSMF.\nAssessment | Integrated Scientific Evidence Assessment | Integrate the intended evidence chain: Cellular → Molecular → Tissue → Human Clinical.",
